<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Intl Lottery rating upped.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Intl Lottery rating upped.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Interstate Johnson Lane has raised its rating on International Lottery to buy from neutral, the brokerage firm said on Monday.</p>
<p>-- ILJ said it issued a 12-month price target of 13 for shares of the Cincinnati, Ohio-based lottery machine manufacturer.</p>
<p>-- ILJ also cut its 1997 earnings estimate to $0.53 a share from $0.77.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
</text>
